          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Pierre\",\"addressee\":\"Hélène\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Je vous aime!\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. Its conventional and embarrassed delivery may bear on sincerity or spontaneity, but it remains an explicit avowal of a loving state.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Теперь уж поздно, всё кончено; да и я люблю ее», подумал Пьер.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.86,\"reason\":\"In this occurrence, the avowal also substantially affirms Pierre's acceptance of the newly established engagement bond. He is already treating Hélène as his fiancée and understands that a conventional relational declaration is now required; thus the expression ratifies or enacts his position as her committed fiancé rather than merely accompanying an unrelated promise. It does not articulate separate terms or a new future-tense promise.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях», думал он\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.97,\"reason\":\"The expression is not represented as a reflex-like affective discharge. Pierre pauses, recalls the socially expected formula, and delivers it so poorly that he feels ashamed; this is deliberate conventional speech rather than an involuntary outburst.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях; но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя.\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"reason\":\"No substantial residual core force is needed beyond avowal and contextual ratification of the engagement. The utterance's socially expected, formulaic quality modifies those forces rather than constituting a distinct mode.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"After Pierre and Hélène have been publicly treated as engaged, their relatives leave them alone. Pierre holds his fiancée's hand; Hélène draws him into a kiss, and Pierre then recalls and utters the conventional words expected on such an occasion. The narration emphasizes his hesitation, social pressure, and embarrassment at the declaration's weak delivery.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"mixed\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal avowal substantially affirms Pierre's acceptance of the fiancé bond already proclaimed around him, but it does not independently specify a new promise or its terms. Hélène's intimate approach and kiss, together with their treatment as an engaged couple, support relational uptake, although the supplied scene does not contain an explicit verbal acceptance from her after this exact utterance. Their later marriage confirms the engagement's continuation but is not itself the focal utterance's uptake.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passages are recognisable as Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace.\",\"limitations\":\"The narration supplies strong evidence of attraction, desire, hesitation, and formulaic social compliance, but it does not conclusively settle the depth or sincerity of Pierre's loving affection. The analysis is limited to the supplied passages and does not assume omitted context is absent from the work.\"}"
        }
